      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using different repository names might also lead to additional issues. With jgit the build started to work after having different bazel repos, but at runtime the dependency version conflict caused errors. I.e. we might miss such issues, if no test hits a break point. Using the same name prevents this, since there is an error on a duplicate dependency. However, this could of course be checked by a simple test that ensures no duplicate entries in both toml-files.\n\nRegarding splitting `/lib`, what about for example `guava`. IIUC Google uses it, but just uses its own version from the build. So I guess it would be fine to reference it everywhere, while lucene probably wouldn\u0027t.",
